meta {
  name: Ban account
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/accounts/actions
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "accountId": {{targetAccountId}},
    "action": "ban",
    "reason": "Banned from the Bruno collection",
    "days": 1
  }
}

docs {
  Omit `days`, or send 0, for a **permanent** ban — AzerothCore encodes that as
  `unbandate == bandate`. Capped at 3650 days.

  The server refuses to ban the account you are logged in as, but nothing stops
  one admin banning another: a banned admin can still drive the SOAP console
  (SOAP does not check bans) yet can no longer log into the portal, which fails
  as a 403 on login rather than a 401.
}
